      "id": 116524,
      "name": "Ronway",
      "username": "Ronway",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-09-02T04:53:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"nkwatts\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nkwatts/48/2404_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> nkwatts:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So why, then, are Victims under Spite's Safe House card still considered Victims?&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Mind revealing what card refers to the cards under Safe House are referred to as Victims?</p>\n<p>The Safe House, Agent of Gloom front and back, and Forced Entry&nbsp;(these being the only ones I can think of that deal with under the Safe House) all refer to them as \"cards under the Safe House\" or something along those lines.</p>\n<p>Edit: I would also like to note that the Safe House is one of the few cards to actually have printed on the card that cards under them have no text, at least the first printing of it does.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
